+//! Stage 4 for one case: each evidence set composed (compose.rs) and summarised for
+//! summary.json.
+//!
+//! Results lead per end-of-flight hypothesis: each descent family of the terminal module and,
+//! when a set uses the terminal module's own data, each option of its alternatives (e.g. what
+//! caused the 00:19 log-on). Each comes with the evidence of the set's data under it. An
+//! average across them is shown only beside a prior sensitivity (the terminal module's own
+//! prior, and a uniform one), because priors such as piloted against unpiloted cannot be
+//! tested. Under a prior pi, P(h | D) is proportional to pi_h Z_h, and the average is the
+//! mixture of the per-hypothesis results with those weights. Every other alternative (the
+//! 00:19 BFO model, an ocean model, ...) is marginalised by evidence within each hypothesis,
+//! and its posterior is reported.
+//!
+//! Every position summary is keyed by the point it describes. Only "contact" (first water
+//! contact) exists now; the acoustic source and the resting place on the seabed will follow.
+
+use crate::compose::{compose, Composition, Replica};
+use crate::config::{ComposeSet, TerminalConfig};
+use crate::summary::{impact_density, map_overlap, overlap, round, round_all, stats, weighted_quantiles, Histogram, IMPACT_MAP};
+use hypothesis::Alternatives;
+use serde_json::{json, Value};
+use std::collections::BTreeMap;
+
+/// The points whose positions the summaries describe.
